#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:1
msgid "ADR-0010: Results, figures and archives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-17"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P7.3 to P7.5 (REQ-RES-1 to REQ-RES-6, NF-7)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:9
msgid ""
"Every run must be traceable (objective O5): the context, the environment,"
" the journal, the figures and the data behind them. The specifications "
"require `vfst.archive` and `pltedit` (VFSciTools) for the archives and "
"the editable figures. PltEdit's `.plt` format pickles matplotlib figures,"
" while LUMOS forbids unpickling user files (NF-7)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:14
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:16
msgid ""
"**VFSciTools is a core dependency** (NF-2): `vfst.archive.new` creates "
"the dated archive directory (`<root>/<date>_<commit>/<NNNN>-<name>/`) and"
" records the UTC date, Python version and git commit and branch; LUMOS "
"adds the other REQ-RES-2 fields to `metadata.yml` (OS, versions of LUMOS "
"and of the key dependencies, hardware report probed once per process, "
"backend, precision, seed, durations, mode, twin, clock, origin, outputs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:21
msgid ""
"**Layout**: `context.lumos`, `metadata.yml`, `lumos.log` (journal as JSON"
" lines), `figures/` (`.png` and `.plt`), `data/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:23
msgid ""
"**Root**: `lumos.config.archive_root`, else an `archives/` directory next"
" to the running notebook (VS Code's `__vsc_ipynb_file__`, Jupyter's "
"`JPY_SESSION_NAME`), else next to the executed script "
"(`__main__.__file__`), else the current directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:26
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Data files**: data products as `.npz` with a JSON header, optical "
"signals as `.json` (`{\"signal\": class, \"data\": to_json()}`), other "
"arrays as `.npz` where a quantity `name` is stored with a string entry "
"`__unit__name`. Every `.npz` is written and read with "
"`allow_pickle=False`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:29
msgid ""
"**Reading back** (`lumos.load_archive`): JSON signals are decoded by a "
"fixed list of classes; `.plt` files are listed, never loaded, since "
"loading them unpickles. Users open them with PltEdit when they trust "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:31
msgid ""
"`ctx.run(outputs, archive=...)` archives the run and every computed "
"output; `result.archive` gives access to the archive to add figures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:34
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:36
msgid ""
"A LUMOS-specific archive directory without VFSciTools: duplicates "
"`vfst.archive` and breaks the convention shared with the author's other "
"tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:38
msgid ""
"HDF5 for all data: an extra dependency for the core; `.npz` with plain "
"arrays is enough and safe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:39
msgid ""
"Loading `.plt` figures in `load_archive`: convenient but unpickles files "
"that may come from someone else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:41
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:43
msgid ""
"~~VFSciTools must be published on PyPI before LUMOS can be installed from"
" PyPI or tested in CI.~~ See the amendment below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:45
msgid ""
"The archive tests probe the real git repository and hardware; the "
"hardware report is cached per process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:47
msgid "Amendment (2026-10-17): VFSciTools is vendored"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0010-results-and-archives.md:49
msgid ""
"Installing LUMOS on Read the Docs and in CI failed because `vfscitools` "
"is not on PyPI. At the author's request, the two parts LUMOS uses are "
"copied into `lumos._vendor` (MIT license, same author): `pltedit` "
"(`save`, `load`, `set_style`; same `.plt` format, the files still open in"
" the PltEdit application) and `vfst_archive` (`vfst.archive.new`). They "
"are kept as upstream except for their imports, excluded from ruff and "
"pyright, and updated by copying them again. `vfscitools` is no longer a "
"dependency; once it is on PyPI, LUMOS may depend on it again and drop the"
" copies."
msgstr ""

